; JEDI INTELLIGENCE: COARSE SNAPSHOTS WITH A DELAYED RESPONSE
; The visible Jedi queries return negative values in controlled engine tests.
; Cheat counts are read ONLY in phase 1, never continuously and never at publish.
; Cadence: initial wait 105s -> sample -> delay 45s -> Hunter window 15s
; -> rest 45s -> next sample. Thus snapshots/publications stay 105s apart.
; A nonzero published warning allows capped Hunter replenishment until replaced.
; Publish only NONE / P1 (small) / P3 (large), retaining existing Hunter targets.
; Hidden losses/reinforcements cannot change a pending or published snapshot.

(defrule
	(goal jedi-intel-phase 3)
	(timer-triggered t-jedi-intel)
=>
	(set-goal jedi-intel-phase 4)
	(disable-timer t-jedi-intel)
	(enable-timer t-jedi-intel 45)
)

(defrule
	(goal jedi-intel-phase 0)
	(timer-triggered t-jedi-intel)
=>
